1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,154
PACT. The payment authorization gateway for AI agents.

2
00:00:04,154 --> 00:00:08,407
Let any agent shop for you, only within the limits you set.

3
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:12,244
AI agents can now shop for us.

4
00:00:12,244 --> 00:00:15,854
But to pay, we hand them a payment method with no limits.

5
00:00:15,854 --> 00:00:19,186
One injected instruction, or one hallucinated price,

6
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:22,491
and real money moves before anyone approves it.

7
00:00:24,583 --> 00:00:27,677
PACT sits between any AI agent and PayPal.

8
00:00:27,677 --> 00:00:29,409
Agents can only ask.

9
00:00:29,409 --> 00:00:32,441
A deterministic policy engine authorizes,

10
00:00:32,441 --> 00:00:35,537
a human approves, and PayPal executes.

11
00:00:36,033 --> 00:00:38,233
It starts with a spending mandate.

12
00:00:38,233 --> 00:00:41,062
This one allows electronics from one merchant,

13
00:00:41,062 --> 00:00:42,988
up to $100 per purchase.

14
00:00:43,483 --> 00:00:45,932
First, PACT's built-in reference agent

15
00:00:45,932 --> 00:00:48,487
is asked for a keyboard that costs $125.

16
00:00:48,487 --> 00:00:50,030
Gemini recommends it,

17
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:52,941
and the policy engine answers immediately.

18
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:56,697
Blocked. Attempted $125. Allowed $100.

19
00:00:56,697 --> 00:01:00,598
There is no approve button and no PayPal order.

20
00:01:00,598 --> 00:01:03,436
The AI can recommend a purchase,

21
00:01:03,436 --> 00:01:07,871
but it cannot override the user's spending mandate.

22
00:01:08,383 --> 00:01:10,497
Next, an eligible request.

23
00:01:10,497 --> 00:01:14,228
Gemini picks an $89 keyboard, and every rule passes.

24
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:17,462
But passing policy is not authorization.

25
00:01:17,967 --> 00:01:19,642
I review the budget impact,

26
00:01:19,642 --> 00:01:21,605
then approve this exact purchase.

27
00:01:21,605 --> 00:01:23,759
My approval is bound to a fingerprint

28
00:01:23,759 --> 00:01:26,403
of the product, the price and the mandate.

29
00:01:26,917 --> 00:01:29,473
PACT creates a real PayPal Sandbox order,

30
00:01:29,473 --> 00:01:32,487
and the buyer approves it in PayPal Checkout.

31
00:01:32,1000 --> 00:01:35,520
Back in PACT, the server asks PayPal directly

32
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,184
whether the buyer approved.

33
00:01:37,184 --> 00:01:39,621
Only then can the payment be captured.

34
00:01:40,117 --> 00:01:41,364
Captured.

35
00:01:41,364 --> 00:01:45,106
A real PayPal capture ID, status COMPLETED,

36
00:01:45,106 --> 00:01:47,116
for exactly $89.

37
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:50,078
What if something changes after approval?

38
00:01:50,078 --> 00:01:51,875
I approve a second keyboard.

39
00:01:51,875 --> 00:01:54,271
Then the merchant raises the price.

40
00:01:54,783 --> 00:01:56,748
The approval is void at once.

41
00:01:56,748 --> 00:02:00,186
A change can never silently inherit an old approval.

42
00:02:00,699 --> 00:02:03,388
Every step is recorded in the audit trail:

43
00:02:03,388 --> 00:02:05,968
the recommendation, the policy decision,

44
00:02:05,968 --> 00:02:09,176
the approval, the PayPal order and the capture.

45
00:02:09,683 --> 00:02:12,627
And PACT isn't tied to one assistant.

46
00:02:12,627 --> 00:02:15,310
Claude, ChatGPT or your own agent

47
00:02:15,310 --> 00:02:18,517
connect through PACT's API or MCP server.

48
00:02:18,517 --> 00:02:22,574
This separate Gemini agent is told money is no object.

49
00:02:22,574 --> 00:02:24,591
PACT still says no.

50
00:02:25,366 --> 00:02:29,484
In the Control Center, every agent gets its own revocable key,

51
00:02:29,484 --> 00:02:31,720
and its requests wait for you.

52
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,073
Agents can ask.

53
00:02:33,073 --> 00:02:36,147
Only you approve, and only PACT can pay.

54
00:02:36,649 --> 00:02:40,095
Agents request. The policy engine authorizes.

55
00:02:40,095 --> 00:02:42,826
A human approves. PayPal executes.

56
00:02:42,826 --> 00:02:47,106
PACT. The payment authorization gateway for AI agents.
